+# Junction review — 2026-11-12
+
+This review takes up the junctions that the street passes deferred. They are pieces of multi-carriageway crossings and roundabouts whose neighbours were already dated. Newly dated length is 145.37 m in 6 persistent objects (EPSG:3874), all new and all first seen in 1968. Three of the objects are lanes, turning pieces or a second carriageway beside road that is already dated, so they count 0 m. The Ålandsplan approaches count once each, as their longest lane.
+
+| Junction | Objects and first evidence | Counted metres |
+| --- | --- | ---: |
+| Godbyvägen–Bolstavägen | 1968: Godbyvägen's carriageways and turning pieces through the junction, with Bolstavägen's eastern leg (17 pieces). 1978: Bolstavägen's western leg (4 pieces) | 0 |
+| Ålandsplan | 1968: the southern half of the roundabout (94.17 m), Skarpansvägen's two lanes at the ring (27.79 m, longest lane), Gesällgatan's leg (23.41 m, longest piece) | 145.37 |
+| Västra Utfarten south of Klintvägen | 1995: the second carriageway through the crossing (3 pieces) | 0 |
+
+## Findings
+
+**Godbyvägen–Bolstavägen.** In 1968 Godbyvägen is a red road through the junction, and Bolstavägen's eastern leg joins it as a double-lined street. The modern carriageways and turning lanes all lie inside that one road symbol, so they start in 1968 together with the dated pieces north and south of the junction, and they add no length. Bolstavägen's western leg is first drawn in the thick red 1978 overprint, like the rest of western Bolstavägen. Its two lanes therefore start in 1978.
+
+**Ålandsplan.** The roundabout, with its round central island, is drawn from 1968 in the same place as today. Part of the ring was already dated. The southern half and the Skarpansvägen and Gesällgatan connections now start in 1968 as well. Skarpansvägen's refuge is first drawn in 1985, but the road lies in the same place from 1968.
+
+**Västra Utfarten south of Klintvägen.** The three undated pieces are the second carriageway through the crossing. The maps draw one road there until 1995. In 1968–1985 the evidence is therefore recorded as *unclear*, and the carriageway starts in 1995 at 0 m, as the west carriageway further north does since the fourth pass.
+
+## Deferred
+
+These are listed in the review file and stay undated:
+
+- **Framnäsvägen and Varvsvägen.** They are drawn as streets from 1985, but they join Västra Utfarten's west carriageway, which the maps do not show separately until 1995. Dated from 1985, they would end 6–9 m short of the network during 1985–1994.
+- **Doktorsvägen's service section (way 77082300).** In 1995 it is a black dashed path, not a red street. Uppgårdsvägen connects northwards via Nya Godbyvägen instead.
+- **The western part of Kråkbärsstigen, Hjortronstigen's link, Mästargränd and Ekogränd.** Today they connect only through footways and cycleways, so they wait for a road-to-path model.
+- **Michaelsvägen's roundabout at Nya Godbyvägen.** It is later than 1995.
+
+## Validation
+
+`junctions/prepare.py` writes `data/mariehamn-junction-review.json` against the snapshot `junctions/before.json.gz`, which is identical to the published catalogue after the fifth pass. The script captures input hashes and is kept for audit, so do not rerun it blindly. The crops `junctions/j*-seq.jpg` show each junction with the undated pieces outlined on 1968, then the unmarked 1968, 1978, 1985 and 1995 editions. `scripts/mariehamn_junction_review.py` runs after the fifth pass and uses the shared `apply_reviewed_streets` (marker `mariehamnJunctionReview`).
+
+`junctions/audit.py` confirms that the baseline equals the snapshot. The review adds 6 objects (36,215 → 36,221), 140 geometries (47,060 → 47,200), all with the review's prefix, and one source. No existing object, geometry or city stage changes.
+
+`tests/mariehamn-junction-review.test.cjs` checks:
+
+- the totals and counting rules;
+- each junction's start and stable geometry;
+- single ownership against all earlier passes;
+- that the deferred ways stay unowned;
+- that each junction joins a road drawn in its first edition;
+- the 1968, 1978 and 1995 starts.
+
+`tests/test_mariehamn_junction_review.py` checks that the review applies once and needs the fifth pass. It also checks that the compiler rejects an early western leg, a second carriageway present before 1995, double ownership, changed inputs and wrong counts.
